SHUTO RUN — Setup & Usage Instructions
========================================

WHAT IT IS
----------
Shuto Run is a standalone single-file browser racing game set on a stylised
Tokyo expressway. You drive endlessly through traffic, dodging cars for points,
with real sampled engine audio, day/night lighting modes, and a full dashboard.

All audio files must be placed in the SAME FOLDER as the HTML file.
If the .wav files are absent the game falls back to a built-in synth engine.

RUNNING THE GAME
----------------
1. Place the HTML and any .wav files together in one folder.
2. Open shuto-run-standalone.html in a modern browser (Chrome/Edge recommended).
   Firefox and Safari work but may have lower audio quality.

   ⚠  Loading from a local file:// URL works fine on Chrome/Edge.
      Firefox may block audio autoplay — click anywhere on the menu to unlock.

3. On the start menu:
     Car         — choose your car (different top speeds and redlines)
     Transmission — Auto / Semi / Manual
     Time of day — Night / Sunset / Dawn / Day (affects lighting)
     Road        — Dry or Wet
     Quality     — Low / Medium / High (affects shadows and resolution)

4. Click START.

CONTROLS
--------
  W / ↑          Accelerate
  S / ↓          Brake / reverse
  A / ←          Steer left
  D / →          Steer right
  Shift           Nitro (uses your nitro bar)
  Q               Shift down (Semi/Manual only)
  E               Shift up  (Semi/Manual only)
  T               Cycle transmission mode (Auto → Semi → Manual)
  C               Cycle camera (chase / bumper / hood)
  V               Toggle wet road
  1 / 2 / 3 / 4  Switch time of day on the fly
  R or Enter      Retry after crash

SCORING
-------
  • Drive as far as you can without crashing into traffic.
  • Near misses (close passes) score bonus points multiplied by your combo.
  • Your combo counter resets after 3 seconds with no close passes.
  • Collecting near-miss points also charges your nitro bar.
  • Hitting a vehicle at speed ends the run.
  • Your best score is saved in the browser's local storage.

ENGINE SOUND FORMAT
-------------------
The game reads any audio file whose name contains a number followed by "rpm"
(e.g. 1000rpm, 2500rpm, 7000rpm) and blends between adjacent samples in real
time. The limiter sound must have "lim" in its filename (engine_lim.wav).

Name your files exactly as listed above or the auto-fetch will not find them.
The game also still accepts the old drag-and-drop file picker if you prefer.

TIPS
----
  • In Auto mode, the car shifts itself focus on steering and nitro.
  • In Semi mode, you must shift up manually but the car downshifts for you.
  • Manual mode: you control every gear change. Rev-matching matters.
  • Wet road reduces grip and makes high-speed cornering harder.
  • High quality mode adds bloom and higher-resolution shadows. 
  • The GT-R Nismo has all-wheel drive (higher grip stat).

